<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cynllaith</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cynllaith was a medieval commote in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, in the valley of the River Cynllaith on the borders of modern Powys and Wrexham. It formed part of Powys Fadog, and its lordship was later held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-glyndwr">Owain Glyndŵr</a>, whose principal house stood at Sycharth within it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cynllaith.jpg" alt="Cynllaith" width="320" height="329" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: my work · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wales.medieval.cymydau.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
